# ft_ls tests

Compares `./ft_ls` to system `ls` on a fixed fixture tree (stdout, stderr, exit code).

```bash
bash tests/run_tests.sh      # quick run
bash tests/run_tests.sh -v   # + valgrind on each case
bash tests/run_tests.sh -k   # keep tests/.work for debugging
```

Run as your normal user (not root), or permission cases are meaningless.

Mandatory coverage: `-l`, `-R`, `-a`, `-r`, `-t`, operands, errors, unreadable /
not-searchable directories, device lines, future file dates.

Not tested (bonus): ACL `+`, multi-column layout, colors, extra options.
